window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Quick Start","u":"getting-started.html#quick-start","x":"The kit works the moment it's imported. No setup is needed for the first report. Open Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Open Demo > Bug Hunt and press Play. Press Deliver the crate . The game throws an error and the crate falls through the floor. The Bug Hunt demo after triggering its bugs Press F8 . The form opens with a screenshot taken just before it, and the steps already filled in. Type what happened, draw a circle round the crate, and press Save report . The report form with a circle and an arrow drawn on the screenshot Stop playing. Open Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Report Inbo"},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"In your own game","u":"getting-started.html#in-your-own-game","x":"Press F8 while playing any of your scenes. That's all. To make it yours: Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Setup Wizard creates the settings, adds your game state to reports and points you to the rest. Press the key above Tab while playing for the debug console, stats and options. In a Development Build the kit is there; in a release build it isn't. See Builds and privacy ."},{"p":"Quick Start","h":"Where reports go","u":"getting-started.html#where-reports-go","x":"On the tester's device, in the game's persistent data folder under BugReports . Each one is a single zip with report.html (opens in any browser), report.json , the screenshot, the replay pictures and the log. Testers send you the zip; you open it in the Report Inbox, or just open the html."},{"p":"Samples","h":"Samples","u":"samples.html#samples","x":"Two demo scenes, in Samples/Scenes . Open either with Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Open Demo . They draw correctly in Built-in, URP and HDRP with no setup, and use only the kit's own shader and plain blocks."},{"p":"Samples","h":"Bug Hunt","u":"samples.html#bug-hunt","x":"You're testing \"Crate Delivery\", a tiny game about to ship with real bugs in it. Press Play, then trigger a bug: - Deliver the crate : the crate falls through the floor and the delivery throws an error. - Collect pay : gold goes down instead of up, and a warning is logged. - Flip the lamp switch : the lamp flickers forever. Press F8 . The form opens with the screenshot taken before it appeared and the steps filled in from what you did. Write a line, mark the screenshot, and save. Stop playing and open Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Report Inbox . Pick the report, click a stack line to go "},{"p":"Samples","h":"Feature Gallery","u":"samples.html#feature-gallery","x":"One button for each thing the kit can do, with the line of code behind it shown after you press it: Open the report form, open the debug overlay, save a report with no form. Switch between the four themes live. Add a recent event, set a game state value, log a warning or an error. Open the overlay (the key above Tab) and look at the Options tab: the spinning block's switch and speed come from [DebugOption] fields in FeatureGalleryDemo.cs with no UI code. In the console, type help , hello Sam or spin off to try the [DebugCommand] methods."},{"p":"Samples","h":"Using the samples in your own project","u":"samples.html#using-the-samples-in-your-own-project","x":"The sample scripts are in their own assembly, so deleting the Samples folder removes them cleanly. Nothing else in the kit uses them."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Adding it to your own game","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#adding-it-to-your-own-game","x":"The kit starts by itself, so in most games there is nothing to do: press Play, then F8. This page is for games that already have their own input, pause menu, cameras, scenes or console, and for the questions that come up when the kit meets them. To check that the kit itself works, open Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Why Isn't It Working while playing and click Open the Form Now . If the button opens the form but F8 doesn't, something in your game is taking the key."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Keys","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#keys","x":"Your game What the kit does What you can do Already uses F8 or the key above Tab Both react Pick other keys in Settings (Open Key, Overlay Key). Set a key to None to switch it off and open the form from your own button with BugReporter.Open() Has a chat box or a name field Ignores its keys while a Unity UI, TextMeshPro or UI Toolkit text field has focus Nothing Has its own text entry, rebinding screen or console Can't see it BugReporter.KeysBlocked = () => myChat.IsOpen; Uses touch gestures A three-finger tap opens the overlay, a four-finger tap the form Switch off Touch Gestures in Settings C"},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Your game's input while the form is open","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#your-games-input-while-the-form-is-open","x":"The form takes the mouse and keyboard, but your game's own input keeps running underneath: typing \"w\" in the form can also walk the player forward. Pause it with the kit's events: void OnEnable() { BugReporter.FormOpened += PauseGameInput; BugReporter.FormClosed += ResumeGameInput; } void OnDisable() { BugReporter.FormOpened -= PauseGameInput; BugReporter.FormClosed -= ResumeGameInput; } void PauseGameInput() => playerInput.actions.FindActionMap(\"Player\").Disable(); void ResumeGameInput() => playerInput.actions.FindActionMap(\"Player\").Enable(); The kit unlocks and shows the cursor while the fo"},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Pausing","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#pausing","x":"With Pause While Open on (the default), the form sets Time.timeScale to 0 and puts the old value back when it closes. If your game sets a time scale other than 0 while the form is open (slow motion, say), the kit keeps it. If it sets 0 (its own pause menu opening behind the form), the kit can't tell that apart from its own pause and puts the old value back; switch off Pause While Open and pause from BugReporter.FormOpened instead if your game pauses itself. The kit itself runs on unscaled time, so the form and overlay work while your game is paused. The overlay's timescale command changes Time"},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Scenes","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#scenes","x":"The kit lives on one hidden object that survives scene loads. A report records the active scene and every other scene loaded next to it. Go to where the tester was opens the same set (asking first if you have unsaved changes) and tells you if one of them isn't in this project. If your game destroys every object on reset, including ones kept with DontDestroyOnLoad, it destroys the kit's too; call BugReporter.Start() after the reset to bring it back. Game state providers on objects that are destroyed are dropped by themselves."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Cameras","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#cameras","x":"The screenshot is always what was on screen. For Go to where the tester was , the kit uses the camera tagged MainCamera, or else the screen camera drawn last (cameras that draw into a texture are skipped). The report names the camera it used. For split screen, a camera rig that isn't tagged, or Cinemachine, tell it which one: BugReporter.TesterCamera = () => localPlayer.Camera; With Cinemachine, give the Unity camera that has the Cinemachine Brain, not a virtual camera."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"UI","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#ui","x":"The form and overlay are drawn on their own Canvases at very high sort orders (31990 and 32000), above almost any menu. They use your game's EventSystem when there is one, and add a hidden one only while one of the kit's screens is showing when there isn't. Your EventSystem and its input module are never changed. Without the Unity UI package the kit uses a simpler form with no markup; Why Isn't It Working says so."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Your own code and assembly definitions","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#your-own-code-and-assembly-definitions","x":"If your scripts are in an assembly definition, add RomanoAssets.BugReport to its references to call BugReporter , DebugOptions or [DebugCommand] . Scripts without one (Assembly-CSharp) see it already. Your calls stay in release builds and do nothing there; you don't need #if around them. Release builds leave out the kit's start-up code, its Unity UI screens, its Input System code and its settings, so nothing starts. [DebugCommand] and [DebugOption] keep their methods and fields when IL2CPP strips code, so commands work in IL2CPP builds too."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Other consoles and error reporting","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#other-consoles-and-error-reporting","x":"The kit reads the log with Application.logMessageReceivedThreaded , which works next to other consoles, Sentry, Backtrace or your own log handler. If your game sets Debug.unityLogger.logEnabled = false , reports have no log; Why Isn't It Working warns about it while playing. To use only the report form next to another console, switch off Enable Overlay in Settings."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Big logs and attachments","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#big-logs-and-attachments","x":"Each log line and stack trace is kept up to 16,000 characters and the kit keeps the last Log Lines of them (1,000 by default). Attachments over Max Attachment Megabytes (50) are left out with a note in the report. Read a save file into memory when your attachment callback runs, rather than while the game is writing it."},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Several game windows on one PC","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#several-game-windows-on-one-pc","x":"Every report file has its own random ID, so several copies of the game (multiplayer testing, ParrelSync) can save to the same folder. Unity sends key presses only to the focused window by default. Put \"Host\" or \"Client\" in the game state so you can tell the reports apart: BugReporter.SetContext(\"Network role\", NetworkManager.Singleton.IsHost ? \"Host\" : \"Client\");"},{"p":"Adding it to your own game","h":"Not covered","u":"adding-to-your-game.html#not-covered","x":"Native crashes and hard freezes can't be reported from inside the game. VR, consoles and phones have not been tested on real hardware; for VR, build your own form with BugReporter.UseForm ."},{"p":"The report form","h":"The report form","u":"report-form.html#the-report-form","x":"Testers open it with F8 (Settings > Open Key), the on-screen Report a bug button, a four-finger tap on a touch screen, or from your code with BugReporter.Open() . The game pauses while it's open (Settings > Pause While Open)."},{"p":"The report form","h":"What testers fill in","u":"report-form.html#what-testers-fill-in","x":"What happened? The only box they must fill. What did you expect? What did you do before? Already filled in from the recent events, so most testers only check it. Category and Severity , from the lists in the settings. An empty list hides that choice. Screenshot , taken just before the form opened, so it shows the game, not the form. Testers can draw a Circle or an Arrow , or Blur something private. Blur replaces the pixels with flat blocks, so what it hides can't be recovered. Undo takes back the last mark."},{"p":"The report form","h":"What gets saved","u":"report-form.html#what-gets-saved","x":"Every part has a tick box, and the form says how much each holds. Unticked parts are left out before anything is written, so they reach no file and no destination. Part What it is Screenshot The marked picture Replay The last few seconds as small pictures (Settings > Replay Seconds) Console log The last lines with their stack traces (Settings > Log Lines) Recent events Scene loads, warnings, errors and your breadcrumbs from the last minute System info Game version, build, Unity version, pipeline, OS, device model, CPU, memory, graphics, screen, quality, language. No user or device name Game st"},{"p":"The report form","h":"After saving","u":"report-form.html#after-saving","x":"The form says Report saved with the file's place, and lists each destination's result. Close it and a short note stays on screen for a moment. With no uGUI package, a simpler form with the same parts and no markup is used."},{"p":"Debug overlay","h":"Debug overlay","u":"debug-overlay.html#debug-overlay","x":"Press the key above Tab (Settings > Overlay Key), or tap with three fingers, while playing."},{"p":"Debug overlay","h":"Console","u":"debug-overlay.html#console","x":"The console with level filters and a command line, and the stats strip at the top right Search finds words in messages and stack traces. Info, Warnings, Errors show or hide each level; the numbers count everything that matches the search. Collapse groups identical lines (same message and stack) with a count. Clear hides what's there now; new lines still arrive. Tap a line for its stack trace, Copy , or Report this , which opens the form with the message filled in. Copy all copies every line shown. The command line runs commands: type help for the list, timescale 0.5 for slow motion, or your ow"},{"p":"Debug overlay","h":"Stats","u":"debug-overlay.html#stats","x":"Frame rate, average and worst frame time, memory and garbage collections, with a graph of the last 120 frames: green within 60 FPS, amber within 30, red above. Settings > Stats Strip: With Overlay, Always or Off."},{"p":"Debug overlay","h":"Options","u":"debug-overlay.html#options","x":"Switches, numbers, choices, buttons and read-only values from your Debug Options Sources and [DebugOption] fields. Pin keeps an option on screen, still working, while the overlay is closed. Keep stats on screen does the same for the stats. A pinned option at the bottom left and the stats strip at the top right, with the overlay closed"},{"p":"Debug overlay","h":"Cost","u":"debug-overlay.html#cost","x":"Closed, the overlay reads two numbers a frame and allocates nothing. Open, it refreshes four times a second."},{"p":"Report Inbox","h":"Report Inbox","u":"report-inbox.html#report-inbox","x":"Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Report Inbox reads the zips testers send you. A report in the Inbox: status, notes, where the tester was and the marked-up screenshot Open Folder lists every report in a folder, Open File opens one, and This PC's Reports lists the ones made on this computer while playing in the Editor. Pick a report on the left. On the right: what happened, the screenshot, the steps, recent events, game state, system info and the log. Blue links under each error open your script at that line, even when the report came from another machine, as long as the script is at the sam"},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Make it yours","u":"make-it-yours.html#make-it-yours","x":"Everything testers see can be changed or switched off, with no code. Start with a preset, then change any detail."},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Pick a look","u":"make-it-yours.html#pick-a-look","x":"Open Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Settings . Set Theme Preset to Studio (dark), Daylight (light), Terminal (green on black) or High Contrast. The report form in Studio, Daylight, Terminal and High Contrast The debug overlay in the same four presets That's it. For your own colours, make a theme asset: Assets > Create > All In One Bug Report Kit > Theme , or one of the Theme (Daylight / Terminal / High Contrast) entries. Assign it to Theme in the settings. Its inspector starts with the preset buttons and a live preview, and warns when words would be hard to read. While playing, a theme ch"},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"What a theme changes","u":"make-it-yours.html#what-a-theme-changes","x":"Setting What it does Colours Dim behind the form, panel, text boxes, buttons, accent (main button, chosen chips, focus ring), text, hints, text on the accent, and the info, warning, error and success colours Font Your own font, or Unity's built-in one Text Scale Every word and row from 80% to 160%. Buttons and chips grow to fit their words Your own images Panel, button and text box sprites, 9-sliced when the sprite has borders, tinted by their colour Keep Own Image Shows a sprite in its own colours instead of tinting it Form Max Width How wide the form gets at 1080p Overlay Side Console on the"},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Display as","u":"make-it-yours.html#display-as","x":"Every status message offers the same choice: icon and short text, icon and full text, short text, full text, icon only, or nothing. Message Short Full Saved Report saved Report saved on this device Not saved Not saved Could not save Error badge (console closed) the count 2 errors 1 warnings Note after the form closes Report saved Report saved on this device Icons take the message's colour: success for saved, error for not saved, error or warning for the badge."},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Your own words","u":"make-it-yours.html#your-own-words","x":"Every word testers read comes from one table. Make one with Assets > Create > All In One Bug Report Kit > Text Table , press Fill With Every Word , and type yours in the right-hand column. Assign it to Text Table in the settings. Empty rows keep the kit's words. For languages, set ReportText.Translate from your localisation code instead."},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Switch things off","u":"make-it-yours.html#switch-things-off","x":"What Where The whole kit in a build Settings > Include In (Development Builds Only, Always, Never) Debug overlay Settings > Enable Overlay Stats strip Settings > Stats Strip: With Overlay, Always, Off Error badge Settings > Error Badge, or Display as None Commands Settings > Enable Commands On-screen Report button Settings > Show On Screen Button Touch gestures Settings > Touch Gestures Replay Settings > Replay Seconds = 0 Any part of a report Testers untick it in the form; Settings > Default Parts sets what starts ticked A status message Its Display as: None"},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Pin things on screen","u":"make-it-yours.html#pin-things-on-screen","x":"In the console's Options tab, Pin keeps an option on screen in a small panel while the console is closed, still working. Keep stats on screen does the same for the stats strip."},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Bring your own UI","u":"make-it-yours.html#bring-your-own-ui","x":"Replace the form with BugReporter.UseForm(yourForm) (implement IBugReportForm ) and the overlay with BugReporter.UseOverlay(yourOverlay) (implement IDebugOverlay ). Your UI gets the same report session, with its screenshot, markup, parts and Submit, so nothing else changes. BugReporter.FormOpened , FormClosed , OverlayOpened , OverlayClosed , ReportSaved and ThemeChanged let your game react."},{"p":"Make it yours","h":"Gamepads and keyboards","u":"make-it-yours.html#gamepads-and-keyboards","x":"Every button, text box and switch shows a ring in the accent colour when selected. The console opens with a tab selected, the form with the first text box, and the result with Close, so a gamepad works from the first press."},{"p":"Builds and privacy","h":"Builds and privacy","u":"builds-and-privacy.html#builds-and-privacy","x":""},{"p":"Builds and privacy","h":"Which builds contain the kit","u":"builds-and-privacy.html#which-builds-contain-the-kit","x":"Settings > Include In: Development Builds Only (the default): there in the Editor and in builds with Development Build ticked; gone from release builds. Always : in every build, so players can report bugs too. Never : switched off everywhere, the Editor included. A build that leaves the kit out really leaves it out: the code that starts it, the Unity UI form and overlay and the input code are removed, and the settings (with any Discord or server address) are not in the build. A small core stays so your own calls such as BugReporter.AddBreadcrumb still compile; nothing starts it, so they simply"},{"p":"Builds and privacy","h":"What leaves the device","u":"builds-and-privacy.html#what-leaves-the-device","x":"Nothing, by default. Each report is a zip in the game's persistent data folder. The kit has no analytics, no telemetry and no account. If you switch them on in the settings: Discord : each report is posted to a channel through its webhook. Anyone with a build can find the webhook address, so use a private test channel. Your own server : each report is sent as a form POST with the zip and a few fields. When a send fails, the zip stays on the device and the kit tries again the next time the game starts, up to five times. The form's privacy line says plainly where reports go, and testers can unti"},{"p":"Settings","h":"Settings","u":"settings.html#settings","x":"Open them with Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Settings . The first time, this makes BugReportSettings.asset in Assets/AllInOneBugReportKitData . That folder is yours: it sits outside the kit, so updating the kit never touches it. Every setting has a tooltip."},{"p":"Settings","h":"Builds","u":"settings.html#builds","x":"Setting Default What it does Include In Development Builds Only Which builds contain the kit. See Builds and privacy"},{"p":"Settings","h":"Look","u":"settings.html#look","x":"Setting Default What it does Theme empty Your own theme asset. Empty uses the preset below Theme Preset Studio Studio, Daylight, Terminal or High Contrast Text Table empty Your own words for everything testers read. Empty uses the kit's English More in Make it yours ."},{"p":"Settings","h":"Opening the form","u":"settings.html#opening-the-form","x":"Setting Default What it does Open Key F8 Opens the report form Show On Screen Button off A small Report a Bug button, for touch screens and gamepads Touch Gestures on Three-finger tap opens or closes the overlay, four-finger tap opens the form Pause While Open on Stops game time while the form is open and frees the mouse cursor"},{"p":"Settings","h":"Debug overlay","u":"settings.html#debug-overlay","x":"Setting Default What it does Enable Overlay on The console, stats strip and debug options Overlay Key the key above Tab Opens and closes the overlay Stats Strip With Overlay When frame rate, frame time and memory show: never, with the overlay, or always Error Badge on While the overlay is closed, a small badge counts new warnings and errors Enable Commands on Lets testers type commands in the console More in Debug overlay ."},{"p":"Settings","h":"Choices in the form","u":"settings.html#choices-in-the-form","x":"Setting Default What it does Categories Gameplay, Visual, Audio, UI, Performance, Other What a tester can pick. An empty list hides the choice Severities Minor, Major, Blocker Same, for severity"},{"p":"Settings","h":"What is captured","u":"settings.html#what-is-captured","x":"Setting Default What it does Log Lines 1000 How many Console lines are kept in memory Breadcrumb Seconds 60 How far back the recent events go Max Attachment Megabytes 50 Attachments larger than this are left out, with a note in the report Default Parts All Parts ticked when the form opens. Testers can still untick them Replay Seconds 5 How many seconds before the report the replay covers. 0 turns it off Replay Frames Per Second 2 More is smoother and uses more memory Hide User Name on Replaces the computer's user name in logs and game state Privacy Note empty The line in the form saying where "},{"p":"Settings","h":"Optional destinations","u":"settings.html#optional-destinations","x":"The zip is always saved on the device. These are off until you switch them on. Setting Default What it does Send To Discord, Discord Webhook Url off, empty Also posts each report to a Discord channel. Use a private test channel Send To Http, Http Url off, empty Also sends each report to your server as a form POST: a report zip plus id , category , severity and summary Why Isn't It Working (same menu) checks these settings against your project and says in plain words what to change."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Extending","u":"extending.html#extending","x":"Everything below works with no compile switches: in builds that leave the kit out, each call does nothing."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Add to every report","u":"extending.html#add-to-every-report","x":"BugReporter.AddBreadcrumb(\"Opened the shop\"); // a line in Recent events BugReporter.SetContext(\"Level\", \"Forest 2\"); // a line in Game state; null removes it BugReporter.AddContextProvider(myProvider); // IReportContextProvider, read when a report starts BugReporter.AddAttachment(\"save.dat\", () => File.ReadAllBytes(savePath)); ReportPrivacy.Redact = text => Regex.Replace(text, @\"\\S+@\\S+\", \"<email>\"); With no code: add a Report Context Source component and list values to read from your components."},{"p":"Extending","h":"Open, save and listen","u":"extending.html#open-save-and-listen","x":"BugReporter.Open(); // the form, with a fresh screenshot BugReporter.Open(\"Boss fight softlocked\"); // with What happened filled in BugReporter.SaveQuickReport(\"Crash in level 3\"); // straight to a zip, no form BugReporter.ReportSaved += result => Debug.Log(result.ZipPath); BugReporter.FormOpened += PauseMyInput; BugReporter.FormClosed += ResumeMyInput;"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Console commands and options","u":"extending.html#console-commands-and-options","x":"[DebugCommand(\"give_gold\", \"Adds gold.\")] static string GiveGold(int amount) { Gold += amount; return \"Gold \" + Gold; } [DebugOption(\"Cheats/God Mode\")] bool godMode; [DebugOption(\"Tuning/Speed\", Min = 0, Max = 20, Step = 0.5f)] float speed; [DebugOption] void ResetLevel() { } void OnEnable() { DebugOptions.Register(this); DebugCommands.Register(this); } void OnDisable() { DebugOptions.Unregister(this); DebugCommands.Unregister(this); } Static commands are found by themselves. With no code: a Debug Options Source component lists values and methods by name. From code: DebugOptions.AddToggle , A"},{"p":"Extending","h":"Your own UI, destinations and input","u":"extending.html#your-own-ui-destinations-and-input","x":"BugReporter.UseForm(IBugReportForm) : your form gets a ReportSession with the screenshot, markup, parts and Submit . BugReporter.UseOverlay(IDebugOverlay) : your console; read lines with BugReporter.GetLog() and watch BugReporter.LogVersion . BugReporter.AddDestination(IReportDestination) : send reports anywhere; the local zip is always saved first. BugReporter.UseKeySource(IReportKeySource) : your own input code for the keys. BugReporter.KeysBlocked : return true while the kit's keys should do nothing, such as while your chat box is open. BugReporter.TesterCamera : return the camera the playe"},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Upgrading","u":"upgrading.html#upgrading","x":""},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"Updating the kit","u":"upgrading.html#updating-the-kit","x":"Back up your project or commit it. Import the new version from the Package Manager (My Assets). Import everything it offers. If Unity reports errors after importing, delete the AllInOneBugReportKit folder and import again: files the new version removed are then gone too. Your settings, themes, text tables, Inbox statuses and notes live in Assets/AllInOneBugReportKitData , outside the kit, so an update never changes them. You can move or rename the kit's folder. It finds its own files wherever they are."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"What changed in each version","u":"upgrading.html#what-changed-in-each-version","x":""},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"1.0.1","u":"upgrading.html#101","x":"Nothing to do. New: the kit's keys are ignored while your game's text fields have focus, BugReporter.KeysBlocked , BugReporter.TesterCamera , Settings > Max Attachment Megabytes, and the \"Adding it to your own game\" page. Closing the form now keeps a slow-motion time scale your game set while it was open, and a cursor your game hid or locked."},{"p":"Upgrading","h":"1.0.0","u":"upgrading.html#100","x":"The first release. Nothing to do. The full list of changes is in CHANGELOG.md in the kit's folder."},{"p":"Troubleshooting","h":"Troubleshooting","u":"troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting","x":"Start with Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Why Isn't It Working . It checks everything the form needs and offers a one-click fix where there is one. What you see Why, and what to do F8 does nothing in the Editor Click the Game view first so it has the keyboard. Check Settings > Include In isn't Never. In Why Isn't It Working, click Open the Form Now while playing: if that works, your game is taking the key (see Adding it to your own game ) F8 or the key above Tab does nothing while typing On purpose: the kit ignores its keys while one of your text fields has focus My game moves or shoots w"},{"p":"Support","h":"Support","u":"support.html#support","x":"Every message gets an answer. Documentation: https://romanoassets.github.io/bug-report-kit/docs/ Discord: https://discord.gg/AmpBDxRAKu (ask in #help) Report a bug: https://github.com/romanoassets/RomanoAssetSupport/issues Website: https://romanoassets.github.io/bug-report-kit/ Email: marklromano@outlook.com In Unity: Tools > All In One Bug Report Kit > Help and Support shows these with Copy buttons, and Copy Support Info copies your kit version, Unity version, render pipeline and platform for your message. This kit is free. If it helps you, a short review on the Asset Store helps a lot."},{"p":"Support","h":"More from Romano Assets","u":"support.html#more-from-romano-assets","x":"The same developer makes other All In One kits for Unity, built, tested and documented to the same standard. All of them: https://assetstore.unity.com/publishers/160196"},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#changelog","x":"All notable changes to this kit are documented here, newest first, in Keep a Changelog style."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"[1.0.1] - 2026-11-08","u":"changelog.html#101---2026-11-08","x":"Safer in existing games, from a second-opinion review of how the kit meets other games' input, pausing, cameras and scenes."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Added","u":"changelog.html#added","x":"The open and overlay keys do nothing while a Unity UI, TextMeshPro or UI Toolkit text field in your game has focus, and BugReporter.KeysBlocked lets your game block them (a chat box, a rebinding screen). Closing the overlay always works. BugReporter.TesterCamera chooses the camera for \"Go to where the tester was\". Without it the kit uses the MainCamera, or else the screen camera drawn last, skipping cameras that draw into a texture. Reports name the camera. Reports list every other scene loaded next to the active one, and \"Go to where the tester was\" opens them too. Settings > Max Attachment M"},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Changed","u":"changelog.html#changed","x":"Closing the form keeps a time scale other than 0 that your game set while it was open, and a cursor your game hid or locked meanwhile, instead of undoing them. Very long log lines and stack traces are kept up to 16,000 characters each; the overlay shows up to 12,000 and Copy copies all of it. Game state providers on destroyed objects are dropped instead of failing. The first console command scan reads only assemblies that use the kit."},{"p":"Changelog","h":"[1.0.0] - 2026-11-07","u":"changelog.html#100---2026-11-07","x":""},{"p":"Changelog","h":"Added","u":"changelog.html#added_1","x":"Report form (uGUI, with a simple fallback when uGUI isn't installed): screenshot taken before the form, markup, category, severity, steps filled in from recent events, and a preview of every part with tick boxes. Each report is one zip: an HTML page, JSON, screenshot, replay of the last seconds, Console log with stack traces, recent events, system info, game state and attachments. Optional Discord and HTTP destinations, off by default, with a retry queue. Debug overlay: console with search, level filters, collapse and Copy All; commands; stats strip and frame time graph; debug options from att"}];
